Updated Run Manual — OkoaFloat_1.0
Here's the corrected version with your actual project path (~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0), plus a couple of safety improvements.

Manual — two terminals

Terminal 1 — Backend
bash

cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/backend
source venv/bin/activate
export PYTHONPATH=.
python3 run.py


Terminal 2 — Frontend
bash

cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user
npm install
npm start


Note: If npm start fails, your frontend is likely Vite, not CRA. Try:

bash
npm run dev
Check which one is correct:

bash
cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user
cat package.json | grep -A 6 '"scripts"'
"start": "react-scripts start" → use npm start

"dev": "vite" → use npm run dev

One command — both in a tmux session
Install tmux first (only needed once):

bash
sudo apt install -y tmux
Then launch both services in one shot:

bash
tmux new-session -d -s okoa -n backend \
  'cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/backend && source venv/bin/activate && export PYTHONPATH=. && python3 run.py; exec bash' \
  \; new-window -t okoa -n frontend \
  'cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user && npm install && npm run dev; exec bash' \
  \; attach -t okoa
What it does:

Creates a tmux session named okoa

Window 1 (backend) — activates the venv, sets PYTHONPATH, runs Flask

Window 2 (frontend) — installs deps, runs the dev server

Attaches you to the session so you land on the backend window

Useful tmux keys once inside:

Key	Action
Ctrl+B then 0	Switch to backend window
Ctrl+B then 1	Switch to frontend window
Ctrl+B then n	Next window
Ctrl+B then p	Previous window
Ctrl+B then d	Detach (session keeps running in background)
tmux attach -t okoa	Re-attach later
tmux kill-session -t okoa	Stop everything
Safer variant — skip npm install on every launch
npm install on every startup is slow. If you already ran it once, use this instead:

bash
tmux new-session -d -s okoa -n backend \
  'cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/backend && source venv/bin/activate && export PYTHONPATH=. && python3 run.py; exec bash' \
  \; new-window -t okoa -n frontend \
  'cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user && npm run dev; exec bash' \
  \; attach -t okoa
Only run npm install manually when package.json changes.

Quick preflight (before launching)
Run these once to confirm everything is ready:

bash
# Backend checks
cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/backend
test -d venv && echo "venv: OK" || echo "venv: MISSING — run: python3 -m venv venv && source venv/bin/activate && pip install -r requirements.txt"
test -f run.py && echo "run.py: OK" || echo "run.py: MISSING"
test -f .env && echo ".env: OK" || echo ".env: MISSING"

# Frontend checks
cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user
test -d node_modules && echo "node_modules: OK" || echo "node_modules: MISSING — run: npm install"
test -f package.json && echo "package.json: OK" || echo "package.json: MISSING"
If ports are already in use
If a previous run left Flask or the dev server hanging:

bash
# Kill anything on Flask's default port (5000)
fuser -k 5000/tcp 2>/dev/null

# Kill anything on the frontend port (3000 for CRA, 5173 for Vite)
fuser -k 3000/tcp 2>/dev/null
fuser -k 5173/tcp 2>/dev/null

# Then relaunch tmux
tmux kill-session -t okoa 2>/dev/null
Save this as a shell alias (optional)
Add to ~/.bashrc:

bash
alias okoa='tmux new-session -d -s okoa -n backend "cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/backend && source venv/bin/activate && export PYTHONPATH=. && python3 run.py; exec bash" \; new-window -t okoa -n frontend "cd ~/Desktop/OkoaFloat_1.0/frontend_user && npm run dev; exec bash" \; attach -t okoa'
alias okoa-kill='tmux kill-session -t okoa 2>/dev/null'
Reload and use:

bash
source ~/.bashrc
okoa        # start both
okoa-kill   # stop both
